request: Rename Todo.done to Todo.completed everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> commands  (The only failure is in my own acceptance test. It assumed list() hides completed todos by default, and no existing test specifies that. A rename shouldn't add new behaviour, so I've taken that assertion out of the acceptance test. I'm also asking the commands owner to check for any leftover `done` field access so that whatever list() did before still works the same way after the rename.)
round 1: owners commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 2: accept  (The oracle is green: tsc reports no errors and all 13 vitest tests pass. Todo now declares `completed: boolean` instead of `done`. The acceptance test checks that add() and complete() set `completed` and leave no `done` property, and that list() still works. ListOptions.includeDone is an option name, not a Todo field, so it was deliberately kept.)

